50 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 40 0 R
/T (No one controls the outcome. Instead, we trust in what can emerge when we listen together with empathy. The purposes of a person's heart are deep waters, and someone with patience can draw them out. This practice involves uncovering not just others' words, but the meaning beneath them, even those meanings hidden from ourselves. The structure might seem constraining, but it ultimately becomes liberating.)
/E (No one controls the outcome. Instead, we trust in what can emerge when we listen together with empathy. The purposes of a person's heart are deep waters, and someone with patience can draw them out. This practice involves uncovering not just others' words, but the meaning beneath them, even those meanings hidden from ourselves. The structure might seem constraining, but it ultimately becomes liberating.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
